{
  "user_id": 4,
  "reason": "Account shows locked with 5 failed logins; check for suspicious activity given malware lure in quarantine"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked to release a quarantined \"scanned document zip\" he believes came from the office copier. Checked: quarantine shows Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-08 08:21 UTC, reason MALWARE, not releasable. Sender is an external domain, not our internal copier, so this looks like a common fake-scanner malware lure. Not released, per KB-007/KB-008. Separately, Q-1004 (invoice from harborview-supplies, spam, releasable) is also in his quarantine. He did not ask about it, so I left it alone. Account: status LOCKED after 5 failed_password attempts on 2026-10-09 13:41-13:56 UTC from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 (New York). No hosting-network sign-ins, no MFA denials, and all recent successful sign-ins have Duo and look normal. This looks like the user mistyping his password, not an attack, but he hasn't mentioned it and hasn't asked for an unlock. Still needed: security team review of the malware message, and checking whether other users got the same docs-share.example lure. The user should confirm he did not open a copy of the attachment from anywhere else. The user is expecting real scans, so the copier's scan-to-email setup may also be worth checking.",
  "reason": "User wants a malware-flagged message released; KB-007 says to escalate, and security should review a possible lure campaign."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email you mean (\"Scanned document 0931.zip\"), but I can't release it. Our mail filter flagged the zip file as malware. It also didn't come from our office copier: it was sent from an outside address (scanner@docs-share.example). Fake \"scanned document\" emails like this are a common way attackers spread malicious files. I've passed it to our Tier 2 and security team to review. Please don't open any copy of this email or attachment if you see one anywhere else. If you already opened one, tell us right away. If you're still waiting on real scans, try scanning again at the copier, or save the scan to your network folder. Let us know if they still don't arrive. One other thing: your account is currently locked after several wrong password attempts this morning. If you need it unlocked, just reply and we'll take care of it.",
  "internal_note": "Quarantine Q-1005: from scanner@docs-share.example, subject 'Scanned document 0931.zip', reason malware, releasable=false. External look-alike scanner lure. Not released, per KB-007/KB-008. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation id 1). Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam) is also quarantined; the user didn't ask about it, so no action taken. Account is locked: 5 failed_password attempts 13:41-13:56 UTC 10/09 from corporate IP 203.0.113.10, NY. No hosting-network sign-ins and no MFA anomalies, so this looks like user error. No unlock requested yet and none queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
